INCIDENT 2026-11-19 00:38Z (Opus2 #6862): Central C: at 0 bytes free; an Engram compile failed with os error 112. Opus2 stopped granting Central runs.
Seen read-only:
- TermAl main target/ about 22 GB (it holds the running termal.exe, NEVER to be cleaned);
- Engram/target about 101 GB;
- Engram/.worktrees 362 entries;
- TermAl .tmp 3375 entries, 36 worktrees with their own target/ (5-15 GB each).
Response (Fable2):
- Engram::Fable asked to free Engram/target and superseded worktrees through its Codex lanes (ebe242f7);
- TermAl Codex owners and Sol-a7bb (for Opus2's and Opus3's lists) remove target/ build output of superseded worktrees with no active run, then superseded worktrees, under "Cleanup deletions" (paths checked, nothing forced; frozen in-flight candidates kept);
- Greg informed in Polish (588693a8).
Reopen Central at about 50 GB free.
Lesson: today's many superseded candidates each left a worktree with a 5-15 GB target/. Owners should remove superseded worktrees promptly, not only at item close. Delete this memory after headroom is restored and the lesson is recorded elsewhere.

Scheduler addendum (Termal::Opus2): before granting any Central compile, check (Get-PSDrive C).Free as well as FreeVirtualMemory, and hold when C: has under about 50 GB free. When a leg ends, ask its author to delete that worktree's target/ build output.
